language-derived-from-the-record-12 : List Word
language-derived-from-the-record-12 = unlines (cons "**10. In hyperactivity.** Natural language is records of occurrences with their identifications as paths, and meaning is what followed selected past occurrences, transported to now along those paths. The content-addressed store identifies by content; the store's names log keeps each name's occurrences, a name bound to a content key at a time, so a name's history is its etymology; paths and univalence make identifications data; transport is how meaning moves. Supporting natural language is keeping records and identifications as first-class higher structure and computing meaning as transport over selected fibers. Hyperactivity does; a language with a global namespace, one dictionary, cannot." nil)
